  "notes": [
    "Storeys come from the eaves height (3DBAG), not from b3_bouwlagen: the cluster mixes 4-storey members (eaves ~12.3 m, 3DBAG says 5 because it counts the attic) and 5-storey members (eaves 14.2-14.7 m). The five-bay layout is the same.",
    "The earlier survey photo type-1-b.jpg (Beek en Hoff 12-2: wide 5.5 m core with two small window columns, storage doors at the outer edges, 3.5 m balcony bays at the ends) is a different sub-design that the footprint cluster also contains; it is not modelled.",
    "Roof: 3DBAG decides gable/hip and the ridge direction per pand; all 63 pilot members have a gable roof with the ridge along the long side.",
    "Cladding is a per-pand variant that BAG/3DBAG do not know: variants.json per area, from looking at the panorama.",
    "Cream bands: variant brick-cream (2026-10-10) is the design of all 13 non-re-clad survey members of Sonderbuur; plain brick is the fallback only."
  ]
